==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Indo-European|snewbʰo-|to marry, to wed|lang=la}}. Possibly cognate with {{etyl|grc|-}} {{term|νύμφη||bride, young wife, nymph|lang=grc}} (English {{term|nymph|lang=en}}), but this is disputed.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈnuː.boː/|lang=la}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|nubo|nūbō|nubere|nūbere|nupsi|nūpsī|nuptum|nūptum}}

# {{transitive|rare|lang=la}} I [[cover]], [[veil]].
# {{intransitive|with dative}} I get married to, [[marry]], [[wed]].
## {{intransitive|of plants}} I become joined, tied or [[wedded]] (to).

